                "text": "Each training grid has several 2x2 blocks of red (2).\nSome of these blocks are turned into teal (8).\n\nLet's look at the blocks and their coordinates or ordering:\nExample 1:\n1 block: at row 1, col 1. It turns to 8. Total blocks = 1, turned = 1.\n\nExample 2:\n2 blocks:\n- (0,0) -> stays 2\n- (1,4) -> turns to 8\n\nExample 3:\n3 blocks:\n- (0,0) -> turns to 8\n- (2,4) -> stays 2\n- (2,7) -> turns to 8\nWait, total 3 blocks:\n(0,0), (2,4), (2,7).\nIndices 1, 2, 3?\nBlock 1 (0,0): 8\nBlock 2 (2,4): 2\nBlock 3 (2,7): 8\nWait! Is it alternating, or right-to-left?\nLook at Example 2:\n(0,0) stays 2, (1,4) turns 8.\nIf sorted left-to-right (or right-to-left):\nEx 1: 1 block -> 8.\nEx 2: 2 blocks -> 2, 8. (left is 2, right is 8)\nEx 3: 3 blocks -> 8, 2, 8.\nEx 4: 4 blocks:\nBlocks at:\n(0,0), (0,3), (3,6), (3,9).\nOutput:\n(0,0): 2\n(0,3): 8\n(3,6): 2\n(3,9): 8\nSo: 2, 8, 2, 8!\n\nEx 5: 5 blocks:\n(0,0), (0,3), (0,6), (2,9), (2,12).\nOutput:\n(0,0): 8\n(0,3): 2\n(0,6): 8\n(2,9): 2\n(2,12): 8\nPattern: 8, 2, 8, 2, 8!\n\nLook at the pattern based on N (total number of blocks) or from right to left:\nIf rightmost is always 8:\nEx 1 (N=1): 8 (ends with 8)\nEx 2 (N=2): 2, 8 (ends with 8)\nEx 3 (N=3): 8, 2, 8 (ends with 8)\nEx 4 (N=4): 2, 8, 2, 8 (ends with 8)\nEx 5 (N=5): 8, 2, 8, 2, 8 (ends with 8)\n\nYes! Alternating colors, ending with 8 at the last block (sorted by position, e.g. reading order or x-coordinate).\nNotice in all examples, reading order (row, then col) and x-coordinate order are identical!\nAnd the sequence of blocks, from last to first, is:\nlast block: 8\n2nd to last: 2\n3rd to last: 8\n4th to last: 2\nand so on!\nOr simply: (N - 1 - i) % 2 == 0 -> 8, else 2.\nwhere i is the 0-based index of the block.Ready for the test grids. Turn your rule into an actionable plan and wait for the test input.",
